I have some sadly really disturbing  numbers to give you about shootings in  America recently I told you we did a  story I think it was about ten days  after the Las Vegas shooting and at that  point a couple hundred people had been  shot in the United States and of course  with much less fanfare much less media  drama than the Las Vegas shooting and I  have some even more really sort of  stunning but also depressing numbers for  you today which is that between the Las  Vegas shooting that took place October  1st and the shooting at the Texas church  that took place just a few days ago in  Sutherland Springs Texas 4319 people  have been shot in the United States and  thirteen hundred and eighty five of them  were killed okay between the two mass  shootings Las Vegas shooting October 1  Texas shooting November 4 Las Vegas 58  people shot dead Texas 26 people shot  dead 84 people total shot dead in those  two incidents tragic horrible absolutely  sickening but the degree of violence  that we're experiencing is unique to the  United States among developed nations  you really have to go to countries that  the US doesn't consider really our peers  to find rates of gun violence and gun  death this high and between the two  shootings which combined took 84 lives  1385 lives were lost in small shootings  and the victims are varied in terms of  age in terms of location in terms of  ethnicity and education income  employment 22 year old black woman from  not too far from from where we are  Pittsfield Massachusetts an 18 year old  Hispanic woman from South Carolina was  shot and killed a 54 year old white  woman in Arizona was shot dead a 37 year  old white man in New York City a 17 year  old asian kid in Georgia shot dead and  why does this matter right it matters  because talking about shootings as one  thing doesn't make any sense I've said  it before and I will say it again there  are mass shootings there  our individual shootings there are  double homicides there are suicides with  guns and we should be trying to prevent  all of them and the ways that we might  go about preventing mass shootings for  example are not the same ways we might  go about preventing individual shootings  which of course kill way more people in  total but fewer people per incident and  that gets me to one of the main sort of  fallacious ways that the pro-gun right  thinks or at least claims to think about  gun safety no matter what proposal gun  safety advocates make right no matter  how well backed by research it is no  matter how well backed by data it is you  will have people who will say hey you  know what that particular method makes  no sense because it wouldn't have  prevented this type of via of gun  violence or that particular shooting  that's not a reason not to do it that's  a reason to do it along with many other  things yes it's true there might be some  tactic or change that could be made  which would prevent or make more  difficult or less deadly mass shootings  but it's true that more than likely the  way to prevent mass shootings is not  going to prevent gun suicides that's a  reason to do different things to prevent  each and not reason to do nothing and  this is becoming more and more common  among the so called gun rights advocates  who appear in the media whatever you  proposed they'll come up with a scenario  and they say hey it wouldn't have  prevented this one if you do that you  wouldn't have actually prevented the  Aurora movie theater shooting he still  could have gotten his guns or whatever  oh here's a way you could have prevented  the Aurora movie theater shooting well  that wouldn't have prevented the Texas  mass shooting because that was a  different type of scenario that just  tells us there's not one solution that  tells us the problem is so deep and so  ingrained in our culture and our society  that there is not going to be one  solution to fix the entire problem  that's a reason to do more not less it's  sort of like when a regulation that is  in place isn't enforced the left says oh  we've got to put more resources behind  actually enforcing it and the right will  say hey see I told you regulations don't  work  cancel all of them it's fallacious  thinking it makes absolutely no sense
 

